{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace measures the driven route at 11.18 km against a booked optimal of 8.2 km — an excess of 2.98 km and 36.34% — both above the 0.8 km and 20% gates in POL-RD-01, so a route deviation is established on this trip's own trace, measured from the trace figure that governs rather than the rounded trip-record copy of the same measurement.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00103", "EV-TRIP-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both charged gantries — CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) at $3.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd towards City) at $1.00 — carry on_optimal_route = false, and the trace passes within 250 m of each (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 40.2 m), so the $4.00 is genuine but off-route ERP, exactly the class of charge POL-RD-09 sends back to the rider when the detour was not the rider's doing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00103", "EV-GPS-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own route carried no ERP at all: optimal_route_erp_sgd is 0.0 on the trip record and the recomputed components show optimal_route_erp of 0, so the whole $4.00 of ERP is a by-product of the CTE diversion and not a cost of getting this rider to the stadium. The rider should not bear a gantry charge that exists only because the car was sent a different way.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00103", "EV-FARE-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "components.optimal_route_erp",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-00103-01 records an emergency all-lane closure on Braddell Road — the road the optimal route traverses — active 05:30–12:00 and overlapping the trip window, so the diversion is an external event under POL-RD-03. The distance and time charges may stand for the driver, but because the rider did not cause the closure either, POL-RD-09(2) requires the off-route ERP to be refunded to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction, and $4.00 is comfortably inside the $12.00 cap.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00103-01", "EV-FARE-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's message 'braddell close today, i take CTE ah' is the driver announcing his own routing choice, and the rider's 'ok' is bare acknowledgement; no instruction issued by the rider names a road or a waypoint and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable on this record and POL-RD-09(3) does not strip the ERP refund away from the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Cross-checking the money on the platform's own figures: the closure-adjusted recomputation in the fare breakdown puts the payable at $4.15 (refund before rounding $4.13) against a charged total of $25.12. So whether the ERP is returned as a POL-RD-09(2) pass-through of $4.00 or the judge runs POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal route for $4.15, the rider is owed about $4 and the $4.00 gantry charge cannot stand in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider: the deviation on this trip is established but excused, and the one charge that should never have reached you is returned.\n\nThe GPS trace records 11.18 km driven against the 8.2 km booked optimal — an excess of 2.98 km and 36.34%, over both POL-RD-01 gates (0.8 km, 20%). But the LTA advisory ADV-20260714-031 (EV-ADVIS-00103-01) records an all-lane emergency closure of Braddell Road between Lorong 1 Toa Payoh and Bishan Rd — exactly the corridor your optimal route uses — active 05:30–12:00 and overlapping your 08:07–08:36 trip, with intersects_route and overlaps_trip_window both true. Under POL-RD-03 the justified excess is min(2.98, 1.30 x (10.6 - 8.2) + 1.00 = 4.12) = 2.98 km, i.e. the whole excess, so the diversion is FULLY exonerated and the distance and time charges stand. POL-RD-02 therefore does not run: it applies only where no exculpatory clause fully excuses the excess, and POL-RD-03 excuses all of it here. The $4.15 in the fare breakdown's closure branch is not applied — it is the POL-RD-02 recomputation against the closure-adjusted optimum, and the $0.15 above the ERP is the distance/time differential that stays with the driver. The driver drove the closure-adjusted optimal: 8.2 + 2.98 = 11.18 km, matching the trace's 11.18 km.\n\nWhat you do get back is the ERP. Both gantries charged — CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) $3.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd towards City) $1.00, total $4.00 — are flagged on_optimal_route=false, and your booked optimal route carries no ERP at all (optimal_route_erp_sgd 0.0). Under POL-RD-09(2), where a deviation is exonerated as an external event under POL-RD-03, the distance and time charges stand but off-route ERP is refunded to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction, capped at $12.00 per trip. $4.00 is inside that cap, so $4.00 is returned. Your 'ok' to the driver's 'braddell close today, i take CTE ah' does not turn this into a rider-requested detour: no rider instruction names a road or a waypoint and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable and POL-RD-09(3) does not take the refund away from you.\n\nDriver: your routing is upheld and you keep the distance and time charges; you are not penalised for a diversion the closure required. Both gantry charges are genuine crossings — the trace passes within 0.0 m and 40.2 m of them, well inside the 250 m match — so this is not a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), and no billing-integrity referral arises. No POL-RD-06 repeat pattern exists (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 553, and the excess is not material at 36.34% / 2.98 km against the 50% / 8.0 km marks), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. POL-RD-04's compensation limb does not fire either: you were billed 11.2 km against a trace of 11.18 km, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall. The only money moving is the $4.00 off-route ERP pass-through, which you never keep.\n\nThe GPS trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (175 fixes at a 10 s interval, coverage 100%, empty gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), so POL-RD-07 does not fire, and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger is engaged: the trip identifiers and timestamps agree across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown, and every charge line has a counterpart. No artifact in this ruling carries a weight below 1.0, so confidence is not capped.\n\nOutcome: PARTIAL_REFUND of $4.00 off the $25.12 charged."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Ruling for the rider in part: a refund of SGD 4.00, being the off-route ERP you were charged.\n\nTo the rider. The closure you described is real and is confirmed by the LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-00103-01: an all-lane emergency closure of Braddell Road (towards Serangoon) between Lorong 1 Toa Payoh and Bishan Rd, active 05:30-12:00 on 14 July 2026, which intersects the booked route and covers your 08:07-08:36 trip. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00103 measures 11.18 km driven against a booked optimal of 8.2 km - an excess of 2.98 km, or 36.34% - above the 0.8 km and 20% gates in POL-RD-01, so a deviation is established. It is exonerated under POL-RD-03: the justified excess is min(2.98 km, 1.30 x (10.6 - 8.2) + 1.00 km) = min(2.98, 4.12) = 2.98 km, so the whole excess is attributable to the closure and nothing remains to refund on distance or time. Those charges stand.\n\nThe ERP is different. Both charged gantries - CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) at $3.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd towards City) at $1.00 - are off the optimal route, and the trace passes within 250 m of each (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 40.2 m), so they are genuine crossings that the closure forced. Because the driver is exonerated as an external event under POL-RD-03, POL-RD-09(2) returns the off-route ERP to you as a standalone pass-through correction: $4.00, inside the $12.00 per-trip cap. That is your refund.\n\nOn your alternative figure of $4.15: POL-RD-02 does not run on this trip. Its gate is a deviation that no exculpatory clause fully excuses, and POL-RD-03 fully excuses this one. The $4.15 is the arithmetic of a POL-RD-02 recomputation (charged_total $25.12 less a closure-adjusted recomputed fare of $20.993, i.e. $4.127 rounded up) that the clause framework does not reach here; the correct vehicle is POL-RD-09(2) and the correct figure is $4.00. On POL-RD-04: the driver's message 'braddell close today, i take CTE ah' was the driver's own announcement and your 'ok' was bare acknowledgement; no rider instruction named a road or waypoint and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable and POL-RD-09(3) does not strip the ERP correction away from you.\n\nTo the driver. The distance and time charges stand, because the closure excused the detour and you drove the closure-adjusted optimal route (8.2 + 2.98 = 11.18 km, matching the trace). The $4.00 is a pass-through of a government-set charge you never keep; it is not a penalty and carries no finding of fault against you. No POL-RD-06 referral fires: this trip's excess is not a MATERIAL deviation (36.34% and 2.98 km, below the 50% and 8.0 km marks) and there is no repeat pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 553 completed_trips_90d). No POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral fires either, because both gantry lines matched the trace.\n\nFigures used: charged_total $25.12; booked optimal 8.2 km; trace distance 11.18 km; excess 2.98 km (36.34%); justified excess 2.98 km; closure-adjusted optimal 11.18 km; off-route ERP $4.00 against a $12.00 cap. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fired: the trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (175 fixes, 10-second interval, empty gaps list, max_gap_sec 0.0), the trip identifiers and timestamps agree across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. Confidence 0.95, above the 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
